id: E6345-draft-2301_80739235
draft: true
title: "Conan 已发布配方冲突时必须用新版本身份重建贡献闭环"
category: conan, registry, ci, successor, pre-pr, metadata
match_keywords: >
  Conan version collision, already published with different recipe,
  version_not_incremented, recipe revision conflict, successor branch,
  package version suffix, Issue PR metadata rebinding, CI L0j
root_cause: >
  The registry rejects a changed recipe under an already published name/version.
  Local Conan and target evidence can be valid while CI L0j still fails because
  the reference is occupied by a different recipe revision. Changing only the
  package directory or PR body leaves the task, branch, Issue, and PR identities
  inconsistent.
error_signature: >
  already published with different recipe|version_not_incremented|L0j.*R37|409
  Conflict.*recipe revision
trigger_tool: conan, gitcode-ci, ohpcd-contrib
phase: ci, successor-prep, pre-pr, post-create
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Preserve the failed PR and its CI result. Confirm all contribution states and
  the upstream source identity, then create a new package-version successor with
  a matching feat/<package>-<version> branch. Rebind every archive path, recipe
  version, task readback, knowledge draft, Issue, PR body, HEAD/TREE, and CI
  record; carry old W3 evidence only as explicitly labeled predecessor evidence.
rec_command: >
  read the L0j log; choose the next unoccupied recipe version; import and claim
  the exact task; create a successor branch; migrate archives/<letter>/<name>/<version>;
  run conan create with the full reference; generate PRE_CREATE; push once; create
  one new Issue and PR; run POST_CREATE, AI Review, CI, and exact-head readback.
verification_cmd: >
  Require the new task row to show the exact package/version, owner, activity and
  branch; require CI to build archives/<letter>/<name>/<version> with L0j PASS;
  compare PR HEAD and CI revision, verify Issue/PR bidirectional linkage, and
  keep the predecessor PR's failure immutable. Do not claim submission until the
  new candidate has same-HEAD CI PASS and a clean latest AI Review.
affected_scope: >
  Any Conan adaptation whose registry reference is already published with
  different recipe bytes, including repairs that preserve the upstream source
  version but require a package-version suffix.
safety_boundary: >
  Never overwrite a published reference, force-push a predecessor, relabel old
  W3 or CI evidence, or submit from a stale branch. A new version identity needs
  a new candidate binding and a fresh authoritative platform readback.
